{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not xs or len(xs) == 1:\n        return []\n\n    # The derivative of c_k * x^k is k * c_k * x^(k-1).\n    # The new coefficient for x^(k-1) is k * c_k, where c_k is xs[k].\n    # So, the new coefficient for x^i is (i+1) * xs[i+1].\n    derived_coefficients = [(i + 1) * xs[i + 1] for i in range(len(xs) - 1)]\n    return derived_coefficients"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "_memo = {}\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the FibFib sequence using memoization.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
